(194, 2, 18, 'Kakunakhai Haor', '250 Hec', 'uploads/images/a6a0131c59977843c5ce5d3f7172dc54.jpeg', 'uploads/images/131b0b3dc52b6b6b467e26b0c5b7366d.jpeg', 'uploads/images/a6a0131c59977843c5ce5d3f7172dc54.jpeg', 'Kakunakhai Haor are special type of Inland Wetlands of Bangladesh situated in the north-eastern zone of the country.', '<p><strong>ABOUT</strong><br />\r\nKakunakhai Haor is a small one, but extraordinarily beautiful. The word Akashi means sky blue color and the word Haor means inundated water body that is created due to overflowing of nearby river.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><br />\r\n&bull; &nbsp; &nbsp;Official Name:&nbsp;Kakunakhai Haor<br />\r\n&bull; &nbsp; &nbsp;District:&nbsp;Sylhet<br />\r\n&bull; &nbsp; &nbsp;Upazila: Gowaninghat<br />\r\n&bull; &nbsp; &nbsp;Area. 250 Hectares.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>LOCATION</strong><br />\r\nSylhet</p>\r\n', '<h1>Geographic Information</h1>\r\n\r\n<p>In a country where one third of all area can be termed as wetlands, the haor basin is an internationally important wetland ecosystem, spread over Sunamganj, Habiganj, Moulvibazar districts and Sylhet Sadar Upazila, as well as Kishoreganj and Netrokona districts outside the core haor area.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>A haor is a wetland ecosystem in the north eastern part of Bangladesh which physically is a bowl or saucer shaped shallow depression, also known as a backswamp. During monsoon haors receive surface runoff water from rivers and canals to become vast stretches of turbulent water.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The total area of haor-type wetland ecosystem in Bangladesh is&nbsp;80,000 square kilometres. The haor basin is bounded by the hill ranges of India &ndash; Meghalaya on the north, Tripura and Mizoram on the south, and Assam and Manipur on the east.</p>\r\n\r\n<h1>Conservation efforts</h1>\r\n\r\n<p>Kakunakhai Haor is a small one, but extraordinarily beautiful. The word Akashi means sky blue color and the word Haor means inundated water body that is created due to overflowing of nearby river. So, combining the two words it means sky blue colored water body. And interestingly the color of the water was really bluish. The clouds from the sky easily reflect on the pristine water from the Haor.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><br />\r\nFew places are occupied with water there. So local people usually do fishing, and probably they will continue until the area dried up totally. Most of the fishing nets are having same design and structure. Also, the style of fishing is a bit different from other area as well.</p>\r\n\r\n<h1>Master Plan of Haor Area</h1>\r\n\r\n<p>The&nbsp;Bangladesh Haor&nbsp;and Wetland Development Board (BHWDB) has taken the initiative to prepare a comprehensive Master Plan with a view to preserve, protect.&nbsp;</p>\r\n', '[{\"image\":\"\\/uploads\\/images\\/131b0b3dc52b6b6b467e26b0c5b7366d.jpeg\"},{\"image\":\"\\/uploads\\/images\\/a6a0131c59977843c5ce5d3f7172dc54.jpeg\"}]', '2023-11-05 16:43:14', '2023-11-11 19:10:01'),
(195, 2, 18, 'Khagra Haor', '757 Hec', 'uploads/images/c3855fa883962bcffdc01c62762b2452.jpeg', 'uploads/images/2857dab8a3e5da8b65001f92f694abb2.jpeg', 'uploads/images/c3855fa883962bcffdc01c62762b2452.jpeg', 'Khagra Haor are special type of Inland Wetlands of Bangladesh situated in the north-eastern zone of the country.', '<p><strong>ABOUT</strong><br />\r\nKhagra Haor is a small one, but extraordinarily beautiful. The word Akashi means sky blue color and the word Haor means inundated water body that is created due to overflowing of nearby river.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><br />\r\n&bull; &nbsp; &nbsp;Official Name:&nbsp;Khagra Haor<br />\r\n&bull; &nbsp; &nbsp;District:&nbsp;Sylhet<br />\r\n&bull; &nbsp; &nbsp;Upazila: Gowaninghat<br />\r\n&bull; &nbsp; &nbsp;Area. 757 Hectares.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>LOCATION</strong><br />\r\nSylhet</p>\r\n', '<h1>Geographic Information</h1>\r\n\r\n<p>In a country where one third of all area can be termed as wetlands, the haor basin is an internationally important wetland ecosystem, spread over Sunamganj, Habiganj, Moulvibazar districts and Sylhet Sadar Upazila, as well as Kishoreganj and Netrokona districts outside the core haor area.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>A haor is a wetland ecosystem in the north eastern part of Bangladesh which physically is a bowl or saucer shaped shallow depression, also known as a backswamp. During monsoon haors receive surface runoff water from rivers and canals to become vast stretches of turbulent water.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The total area of haor-type wetland ecosystem in Bangladesh is&nbsp;80,000 square kilometres. The haor basin is bounded by the hill ranges of India &ndash; Meghalaya on the north, Tripura and Mizoram on the south, and Assam and Manipur on the east.</p>\r\n\r\n<h1>Conservation efforts</h1>\r\n\r\n<p>Khagra Haor is a small one, but extraordinarily beautiful. The word Akashi means sky blue color and the word Haor means inundated water body that is created due to overflowing of nearby river. So, combining the two words it means sky blue colored water body. And interestingly the color of the water was really bluish. The clouds from the sky easily reflect on the pristine water from the Haor.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><br />\r\nFew places are occupied with water there. So local people usually do fishing, and probably they will continue until the area dried up totally. Most of the fishing nets are having same design and structure. Also, the style of fishing is a bit different from other area as well.</p>\r\n\r\n<h1>Master Plan of Haor Area</h1>\r\n\r\n<p>The&nbsp;Bangladesh Haor&nbsp;and Wetland Development Board (BHWDB) has taken the initiative to prepare a comprehensive Master Plan with a view to preserve, protect.&nbsp;</p>\r\n', '[{\"image\":\"\\/uploads\\/images\\/c3855fa883962bcffdc01c62762b2452.jpeg\"},{\"image\":\"\\/uploads\\/images\\/2857dab8a3e5da8b65001f92f694abb2.jpeg\"},{\"image\":\"\\/uploads\\/images\\/974773d3b48a613dfa5f5bb80903f214.jpeg\"}]', '2023-11-05 16:44:35', '2023-11-11 19:09:31'),
(196, 4, 32, 'Hail Haor', '4,918 Hec', 'uploads/images/f297d3020ea0b6f091c18c6e8d902689.jpeg', 'uploads/images/912aeb8b52ced8c8e30c8660a4458b43.jpeg', 'uploads/images/615ad361b128fcfb9e97ffd5a55d05b7.jpeg', 'Hail Haor Wildlife Sanctuary is a major wildlife sanctuary in Bangladesh. It is one of the most important wetlands in the Sylhet Basin for the resident and migratory waterfowls. It is also important watersource for the inhabitants living around when all other sources dry up during summer.', '<h3>ABOUT</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Hakaluki Haor is a marsh wetland ecosystem of north-eastern Bangladesh. It is one of Bangladesh&#39;s largest and one of Asia&#39;s large marsh wetland resources.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Official name: Hail Haor.</li>\r\n	<li>District: Moulvibazar</li>\r\n	<li>Area. 4,918 &nbsp;Hectares.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>LOCATION</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Sylhet</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>AREA</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>The water of the wetland extends to cover approximately 14,000 ha (140 km2) during the monsoon and shrinks to 3,000 ha (30 km2) during the summer season. It is restricted to 130 beels and narrow canals. There are about 172000 people living in 62 villages around the wetland.</p>\r\n', '<h1><strong>Geographic Information</strong></h1>\r\n\r\n<p>Hail Haor is situated in Moulvibazar District. It is one of the notable wetlands of Bangladesh. This is one of the safest abodes of many wild animals and migratory birds. Hail Haor Wildlife Sanctuary is a major wildlife sanctuary in Bangladesh. It is one of the most important wetlands in the Sylhet Basin for the resident and migratory waterfowls. It is also an important water source for the inhabitants living around when all other sources dry up during summer. The sanctuary is located in Moulvibazar District, in the northeast region of the country.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The sanctuary is located mainly between the hills on the south, west, and east side and Manu and Kushiara river plains on the north. The hills are covered with tea gardens and natural forest blocks. The water of the wetland extends to cover approximately 14,000 ha (140 km2) during the monsoon and shrinks to 3,000 ha (30 km2) during the summer season. It is restricted to 130 beels and narrow canals. There are about 172000 people living in 62 villages around the wetland.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The receding water after monsoon exposes the land which is converted to rice fields by local people. The Bangladesh Government and the United States Agency for International Development implemented a project called &#39;Management of Aquatic ecosystems through Community Husbandry&#39; from 1998 to 2008. This project involved local groups in wetland conservation, restoration, and management.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>It is located 3 kilometers (1.9 mi) north-west of Srimangal and 14 kilometers (8.7 mi) southwest of Moulavibazar.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://amarhaor.com/uploads/images/Hail haor 3_1699185184.jpg\" style=\"height:437px; width:656px\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<h1>Hail hour with the chirping of migratory birds: -</h1>\r\n\r\n<p>Small boats drifting through the endless waters. Sitting in those boats, some are fishing, while others are busy organizing fishing. Medium-sized boats move slowly through the water. They are not fishing boats; they are tourist boats.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Tourists come here to watch the sunset in the mellow calm waters. The sky is crimson in the light of the crimson sun in the late autumn afternoon. Shepherds are returning home with their cows. Fishermen are crowding the boats on the shore. A group of fishermen is walking towards the village market with a net on one side and a basket of fish on the other side of the boat. Flocks of birds are running from one end to the other. The surroundings are full of chirping of domestic and foreign birds.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>And after a while the red sun will set. Evening will come. I was talking about Hail Haor of Srimangal in Moulvibazar. Hail Haor is spread across Sadar and Srimangal upazilas of Moulvibazar district and Bahubal upazila of Habiganj district of Sylhet division.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>It has 14 bils and 13 drains. The total area of this haor is 10,000 hectares, of which 4,000 hectares are floodplains, 4,517 ha haor, 1,400 ha beel, 40 ha canal and 50 ha river.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://amarhaor.com/uploads/images/Chayer Haor 1_1699185307.jpg\" style=\"height:392px; width:645px\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<h1>How To Go</h1>\r\n\r\n<p>You can go directly to Srimangal from Dhaka by road and rail. However, after reaching Sylhet by air, you can also come to Srimangal from there.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n', '[{\"image\":\"\\/uploads\\/images\\/efc4cfc19572d8e6cef7303f5ecdc3b0.jpeg\"},{\"image\":\"\\/uploads\\/images\\/f297d3020ea0b6f091c18c6e8d902689.jpeg\"},{\"image\":\"\\/uploads\\/images\\/912aeb8b52ced8c8e30c8660a4458b43.jpeg\"},{\"image\":\"\\/uploads\\/images\\/6468d6b475cf7f493c18e5b870b986e2.jpeg\"},{\"image\":\"\\/uploads\\/images\\/615ad361b128fcfb9e97ffd5a55d05b7.jpeg\"}]', '2023-11-05 19:01:19', '2023-11-06 22:18:18'),
(197, 4, 34, 'Hail Haor', '10,220 Hec', 'uploads/images/d1fd3f46cb6f908f126ac180d8f003b8.jpeg', 'uploads/images/c7a2013b57b12f9a7c1b29e061c80cfa.jpeg', 'uploads/images/871bc933c04753c96e0392a9d661a5a6.jpeg', 'Hail Haor Wildlife Sanctuary is a major wildlife sanctuary in Bangladesh. It is one of the most important wetlands in the Sylhet Basin for the resident and migratory waterfowls. It is also important watersource for the inhabitants living around when all other sources dry up during summer.', '<h3>ABOUT</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Hakaluki Haor is a marsh wetland ecosystem of north-eastern Bangladesh. It is one of Bangladesh&#39;s largest and one of Asia&#39;s large marsh wetland resources.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Official name: Hail Haor.</li>\r\n	<li>District: Moulvibazar</li>\r\n	<li>Area. 10,220 Hectares.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>LOCATION</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Moulvibazar.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>AREA</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>The water of the wetland extends to cover approximately 14,000 ha (140 km2) during the monsoon and shrinks to 3,000 ha (30 km2) during the summer season. It is restricted to 130 beels and narrow canals. There are about 172000 people living in 62 villages around the wetland.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n', '<h1><strong>Geographic Information</strong></h1>\r\n\r\n<p>Hail Haor is situated in Moulvibazar District. It is one of the notable wetlands of Bangladesh. This is one of the safest abodes of many wild animals and migratory birds. Hail Haor Wildlife Sanctuary is a major wildlife sanctuary in Bangladesh. It is one of the most important wetlands in the Sylhet Basin for the resident and migratory waterfowls. It is also an important water source for the inhabitants living around when all other sources dry up during summer. The sanctuary is located in Moulvibazar District, in the northeast region of the country.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The sanctuary is located mainly between the hills on the south, west, and east side and Manu and Kushiara river plains on the north. The hills are covered with tea gardens and natural forest blocks. The water of the wetland extends to cover approximately 14,000 ha (140 km2) during the monsoon and shrinks to 3,000 ha (30 km2) during the summer season. It is restricted to 130 beels and narrow canals. There are about 172000 people living in 62 villages around the wetland.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The receding water after monsoon exposes the land which is converted to rice fields by local people. The Bangladesh Government and the United States Agency for International Development implemented a project called &#39;Management of Aquatic ecosystems through Community Husbandry&#39; from 1998 to 2008. This project involved local groups in wetland conservation, restoration, and management.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>It is located 3 kilometers (1.9 mi) north-west of Srimangal and 14 kilometers (8.7 mi) southwest of Moulavibazar.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://amarhaor.com/uploads/images/Hail%20haor%203_1699185184.jpg\" style=\"height:429px; width:645px\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<h1><strong>Hail hour with the chirping of migratory birds: -</strong></h1>\r\n\r\n<p>Small boats drifting through the endless waters. Sitting in those boats, some are fishing, while others are busy organizing fishing. Medium-sized boats move slowly through the water. They are not fishing boats; they are tourist boats.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Tourists come here to watch the sunset in the mellow calm waters. The sky is crimson in the light of the crimson sun in the late autumn afternoon. Shepherds are returning home with their cows. Fishermen are crowding the boats on the shore. A group of fishermen is walking towards the village market with a net on one side and a basket of fish on the other side of the boat. Flocks of birds are running from one end to the other. The surroundings are full of chirping of domestic and foreign birds.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>And after a while the red sun will set. Evening will come. I was talking about Hail Haor of Srimangal in Moulvibazar. Hail Haor is spread across Sadar and Srimangal upazilas of Moulvibazar district and Bahubal upazila of Habiganj district of Sylhet division.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>It has 14 bils and 13 drains. The total area of this haor is 10,000 hectares, of which 4,000 hectares are floodplains, 4,517 ha haor, 1,400 ha beel, 40 ha canal and 50 ha river.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://amarhaor.com/uploads/images/1eedc2bc842644ac1e008665e630523f.jpeg\" style=\"height:323px; width:645px\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<h1><strong>How To Go</strong></h1>\r\n\r\n<p>You can go directly to Srimangal from Dhaka by road and rail. However, after reaching Sylhet by air, you can also come to Srimangal from there.</p>\r\n', '[{\"image\":\"\\/uploads\\/images\\/d1fd3f46cb6f908f126ac180d8f003b8.jpeg\"},{\"image\":\"\\/uploads\\/images\\/c7a2013b57b12f9a7c1b29e061c80cfa.jpeg\"},{\"image\":\"\\/uploads\\/images\\/3676dbc8861bfc93b8334ccd292468be.jpeg\"},{\"image\":\"\\/uploads\\/images\\/871bc933c04753c96e0392a9d661a5a6.jpeg\"}]', '2023-11-05 19:05:57', '2023-11-06 22:17:42'),
(198, 6, 35, 'Borkha Khila bandh Haor', '3,480 Hec', 'uploads/images/ad1f62276162d427305dfb8c5be3fb1f.jpeg', 'uploads/images/7c605a2221f711a91541036febbc37a7.jpeg', 'uploads/images/7c605a2221f711a91541036febbc37a7.jpeg', 'Borkha Khila bandh Haor are special type of Inland Wetlands of Bangladesh situated in the north-eastern zone of the country. Astagram Haor is a massive water world all around and few island like villages amid of the water. You may find few fishing boats available. Only the island like villages would be around you, nothing else. It would be the best way to explore the Haor in the rainy season from the Ostogram. ', '<p><strong>ABOUT</strong><br />\r\nBorkha Khila bandh Haor is&nbsp; extraordinarily beautiful. The word Akashi means sky blue color and the word Haor means inundated water body that is created due to overflowing of nearby river.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><br />\r\n&bull; &nbsp; &nbsp;Official Name:&nbsp;Borkha Khila bandh Haor<br />\r\n&bull; &nbsp; &nbsp;District:&nbsp;Kishoreganj<br />\r\n&bull; &nbsp; &nbsp;Upazila: Austagram<br />\r\n&bull; &nbsp; &nbsp;Area. 3,480 Hectares.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>LOCATION</strong><br />\r\nKishoreganj</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n', '<h1>Geographic Information</h1>\r\n\r\n<p>In a country where one third of all area can be termed as wetlands, the haor basin is an internationally important wetland ecosystem, spread over Sunamganj, Habiganj, Moulvibazar districts and Sylhet Sadar Upazila, as well as Kishoreganj and Netrokona districts outside the core haor area.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>A haor is a wetland ecosystem in the north eastern part of Bangladesh which physically is a bowl or saucer shaped shallow depression, also known as a backswamp. During monsoon haors receive surface runoff water from rivers and canals to become vast stretches of turbulent water.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The total area of haor-type wetland ecosystem in Bangladesh is&nbsp;80,000 square kilometres. The haor basin is bounded by the hill ranges of India &ndash; Meghalaya on the north, Tripura and Mizoram on the south, and Assam and Manipur on the east.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Astagram Haor is a massive water world all around and few island like villages amid of the water. You may find few fishing boats available. Only the island like villages would be around you, nothing else. It would be the best way to explore the Haor in the rainy season from the Ostogram. For your information, six of the Upazila of Kishoreganj hold a massive Haor all together. This Haor is further extended with the Haor(হাওড়) from Netrakona, Hobiganj, and Sunamganj district. During the rainy season you can easily move from one Haor to another without interruption.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>the Itna Upazila of Kishoreganj district. It would be around 8/9 hours to reach at the final destination. Which means 8:00 at night if you start at 12 pm, noon. You can hire the boat from the Kuliar Char of Kishoreganj District.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://amarhaor.com/uploads/images/Projects_1699347734.jpg\" style=\"height:344px; width:656px\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Life in a Haor is not that much easy. It is always surrounded by the water during rainy season. Its a big problem for them and they are in a predicament with this massive water. It gives them a facility to travel easily using a boat. So during the rainy season they can travel from one place to another very easily. Even local people from there use to arrange the marriage ceremony during this particular time for the better communication.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>But they can not do any cultivation during this rainy period. They only depend on the fishing and no other works. All the cultivating activities are done during the dry season(locally known as late autumn), and its only once in a year. They use to cultivate for one season and use to run their family with that little amount of grains throughout the year. But during this dry season, their main transportation is walking. No other option is available. So they are confused to decide about which season is better for them. A common proverb from the Haor region is:<br />\r\nIt is very hard to find an ample amount of empty spaces from the villages (or should say islands?) of Haor.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Everything is tightly packed and very much congested. The lavatory, kitchen, house, and all the other stuffs are in the same place. Even the domestic animals are also living so closely with them. It looks beautiful from far, specially when you are sitting on a boat and traveling. But practically its too much dirty all around and they are accustomed to this.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The sewerage water from the lavatory is dropping at the water beside their house. They are having a bath on the same water beside the sewerage dropping zone. Even they are also cleaning their dishes and taking water for cooking from the same place. They can use the tube well water, but they somehow like the water from Haor(হাওর) as it is iron and arsenic free. You can enjoy their daily life works and household works from the boat easily.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>After reaching at the Astagram(অষ্টগ্র্রাম), you can pay a visit to&nbsp;the Kutub Shah Mosque(কুতুব শাহ মসজিদ) from there. A launch service uses to run between Astagram(অষ্টগ্র্রাম) and Kuliarchor(কুলিয়ারচর). Its in every hour or subject to every two hours. Anyone can take the service from those small ships as well.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://amarhaor.com/uploads/images/Mosjid_1699703531.jpg\" style=\"height:328px; width:656px\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<h1>Master Plan of Haor Area</h1>\r\n\r\n<p>The&nbsp;Bangladesh Haor&nbsp;and Wetland Development Board (BHWDB) has taken the initiative to prepare a comprehensive Master Plan with a view to preserve, protect.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<h1>How to go</h1>\r\n\r\n<p>There are several ways you can enjoy the Haor (হাওর) from Kishoreganj district (কিশোরগঞ্জ জেলা). In fact you&rsquo;ll find lot of other places to enjoy the immensity of the Haor (হাওর). For example Nikli (নিকলী), Mithamoin (মিঠামইন), Itna (ইটনা) are the other places at where you&rsquo;ll find the same thing. But if you are planning to enjoy the Haor (হাওর) from Astagram (অষ্টগ্র্রাম), then here are the steps.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>It is obvious that you have to hire a boat for this particular tour. Also you can ride on the local public launches as a passenger, but I&rsquo;ll not recommend that for you. That&rsquo;s a passenger ship, you won&rsquo;t enjoy it as lot of curious eyes will always focus you and record your activities inside their memory. So better hire a boat, and it can be found at Kuliarchor (কুলিয়ারচর), Bajitpur (বাজিতপুর), or even at Bhoirob bazar (ভৈরব বাজার). Just decide from where you want to hire it and how far you want to go. GPS coordinate of the Kuliarchor (কুলিয়ারচর) is (24&deg; 9&rsquo;5.03&Prime;N, 90&deg;56&rsquo;2.62&Prime;E).</p>\r\n\r\n<p>You have to pay total 2200 taka for the round trip from Kuliarchor (কুলিয়ারচর) and Astagram (অষ্টগ্র্রাম). In your case it can be similar, but keep in mind that it can be around 2500-3000 Taka based on the boat&rsquo;s availability as well as your ostentatious &lsquo;city boy&rsquo; behavior. It takes around 2 hours and 15 minutes to reach at Astagram (অষ্টগ্র্রাম). During returning it took less than 2 hours. Probably 110 minutes as it was returning with the flow of the water. GPS Coordinate of the Astagram (অষ্টগ্র্রাম) is (24&deg;16&rsquo;35.39&Prime;N, 91&deg; 7&rsquo;17.99&Prime;Ed)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Where to Stay</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>1. Hotel Tepantor Princess</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Jamirdia Master Bari, Bhaluka<br />\r\nMymenshingh, 2240 Purura, Bangladesh</p>\r\n\r\n<p>2. Hotel River View<br />\r\nStation Road, Kishoreganj</p>\r\n\r\n<p>3. Hotel shahina (Resident)<br />\r\nStation Road, Kishoreganj</p>\r\n\r\n<p>4. Bangladesh Guest House<br />\r\nStation Road, Kishoreganj</p>\r\n\r\n<p>5. Hotel Gangchil (Resident)<br />\r\nStation Road, Kishoreganj</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Things to do</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>The village is really wonderful for its scenic beauty. You can enjoy the gentle breeze that hits on the face after kissing the surface of the water. If you are a traveler, then you will always find out every bit of our traveling, interesting.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Eating Facilities</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>As well as you can find many more restaurant here for food.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Travel Tips</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Do not try to stay in the Haor at evening for it would be safe for you.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n', '[{\"image\":\"\\/uploads\\/images\\/7c671207bee9e8511a0c5b6ab86a92ba.jpeg\"},{\"image\":\"\\/uploads\\/images\\/2961bfc112543ef0569912ab3e9b36f1.jpeg\"},{\"image\":\"\\/uploads\\/images\\/a3c2bf310c5676a4b986a70c4f3b8e62.jpeg\"},{\"image\":\"\\/uploads\\/images\\/d299adbef315ea34c5c5d19d83f25f8f.jpeg\"}]', '2023-11-05 19:34:35', '2023-11-11 18:56:26'),
(199, 6, 35, 'Boro Haor (Austagram)', '2,741 Hec', 'uploads/images/a1d7da3fee92c8b8fe4c3d9c73a6f24b.jpeg', 'uploads/images/4e610bd49f70516dd49ac111fb4550ef.jpeg', 'uploads/images/650b0ecdeb6f324fb441b5155b9828c6.jpeg', 'Boro Haor (Austagram) are special type of Inland Wetlands of Bangladesh situated in the north-eastern zone of the country. Astagram Haor is a massive water world all around and few island like villages amid of the water. You may find few fishing boats available. Only the island like villages would be around you, nothing else. It would be the best way to explore the Haor in the rainy season from the Ostogram. ', '<p><strong>ABOUT</strong><br />\r\nBoro Haor (Austagram) is a small one, but extraordinarily beautiful. The word Akashi means sky blue color and the word Haor means inundated water body that is created due to overflowing of nearby river.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><br />\r\n&bull; &nbsp; &nbsp;Official Name:&nbsp;Boro Haor (Austagram)<br />\r\n&bull; &nbsp; &nbsp;District:&nbsp;Kishoreganj<br />\r\n&bull; &nbsp; &nbsp;Upazila: Austagram<br />\r\n&bull; &nbsp; &nbsp;Area. 2,741 Hectares.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>LOCATION</strong><br />\r\nKishoreganj</p>\r\n', '<h1>Geographic Information</h1>\r\n\r\n<p>In a country where one third of all area can be termed as wetlands, the haor basin is an internationally important wetland ecosystem, spread over Sunamganj, Habiganj, Moulvibazar districts and Sylhet Sadar Upazila, as well as Kishoreganj and Netrokona districts outside the core haor area.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>A haor is a wetland ecosystem in the north eastern part of Bangladesh which physically is a bowl or saucer shaped shallow depression, also known as a backswamp. During monsoon haors receive surface runoff water from rivers and canals to become vast stretches of turbulent water.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The total area of haor-type wetland ecosystem in Bangladesh is&nbsp;80,000 square kilometres. The haor basin is bounded by the hill ranges of India &ndash; Meghalaya on the north, Tripura and Mizoram on the south, and Assam and Manipur on the east.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Astagram Haor is a massive water world all around and few island like villages amid of the water. You may find few fishing boats available. Only the island like villages would be around you, nothing else. It would be the best way to explore the Haor in the rainy season from the Ostogram. For your information, six of the Upazila of Kishoreganj hold a massive Haor all together. This Haor is further extended with the Haor(হাওড়) from Netrakona, Hobiganj, and Sunamganj district. During the rainy season you can easily move from one Haor to another without interruption.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>the Itna Upazila of Kishoreganj district. It would be around 8/9 hours to reach at the final destination. Which means 8:00 at night if you start at 12 pm, noon. You can hire the boat from the Kuliar Char of Kishoreganj District.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://amarhaor.com/uploads/images/Projects_1699347734.jpg\" style=\"height:344px; width:656px\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Life in a Haor is not that much easy. It is always surrounded by the water during rainy season. Its a big problem for them and they are in a predicament with this massive water. It gives them a facility to travel easily using a boat. So during the rainy season they can travel from one place to another very easily. Even local people from there use to arrange the marriage ceremony during this particular time for the better communication.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>But they can not do any cultivation during this rainy period. They only depend on the fishing and no other works. All the cultivating activities are done during the dry season(locally known as late autumn), and its only once in a year. They use to cultivate for one season and use to run their family with that little amount of grains throughout the year. But during this dry season, their main transportation is walking. No other option is available. So they are confused to decide about which season is better for them. A common proverb from the Haor region is:<br />\r\nIt is very hard to find an ample amount of empty spaces from the villages (or should say islands?) of Haor.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Everything is tightly packed and very much congested. The lavatory, kitchen, house, and all the other stuffs are in the same place. Even the domestic animals are also living so closely with them. It looks beautiful from far, specially when you are sitting on a boat and traveling. But practically its too much dirty all around and they are accustomed to this.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The sewerage water from the lavatory is dropping at the water beside their house. They are having a bath on the same water beside the sewerage dropping zone. Even they are also cleaning their dishes and taking water for cooking from the same place. They can use the tube well water, but they somehow like the water from Haor(হাওর) as it is iron and arsenic free. You can enjoy their daily life works and household works from the boat easily.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>After reaching at the Astagram(অষ্টগ্র্রাম), you can pay a visit to&nbsp;the Kutub Shah Mosque(কুতুব শাহ মসজিদ) from there. A launch service uses to run between Astagram(অষ্টগ্র্রাম) and Kuliarchor(কুলিয়ারচর). Its in every hour or subject to every two hours. Anyone can take the service from those small ships as well.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://amarhaor.com/uploads/images/Mosjid_1699703531.jpg\" style=\"height:328px; width:656px\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<h1>Master Plan of Haor Area</h1>\r\n\r\n<p>The&nbsp;Bangladesh Haor&nbsp;and Wetland Development Board (BHWDB) has taken the initiative to prepare a comprehensive Master Plan with a view to preserve, protect.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<h1>How to go</h1>\r\n\r\n<p>There are several ways you can enjoy the Haor (হাওর) from Kishoreganj district (কিশোরগঞ্জ জেলা). In fact you&rsquo;ll find lot of other places to enjoy the immensity of the Haor (হাওর). For example Nikli (নিকলী), Mithamoin (মিঠামইন), Itna (ইটনা) are the other places at where you&rsquo;ll find the same thing. But if you are planning to enjoy the Haor (হাওর) from Astagram (অষ্টগ্র্রাম), then here are the steps.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>It is obvious that you have to hire a boat for this particular tour. Also you can ride on the local public launches as a passenger, but I&rsquo;ll not recommend that for you. That&rsquo;s a passenger ship, you won&rsquo;t enjoy it as lot of curious eyes will always focus you and record your activities inside their memory. So better hire a boat, and it can be found at Kuliarchor (কুলিয়ারচর), Bajitpur (বাজিতপুর), or even at Bhoirob bazar (ভৈরব বাজার). Just decide from where you want to hire it and how far you want to go. GPS coordinate of the Kuliarchor (কুলিয়ারচর) is (24&deg; 9&rsquo;5.03&Prime;N, 90&deg;56&rsquo;2.62&Prime;E).</p>\r\n\r\n<p>You have to pay total 2200 taka for the round trip from Kuliarchor (কুলিয়ারচর) and Astagram (অষ্টগ্র্রাম). In your case it can be similar, but keep in mind that it can be around 2500-3000 Taka based on the boat&rsquo;s availability as well as your ostentatious &lsquo;city boy&rsquo; behavior. It takes around 2 hours and 15 minutes to reach at Astagram (অষ্টগ্র্রাম). During returning it took less than 2 hours. Probably 110 minutes as it was returning with the flow of the water. GPS Coordinate of the Astagram (অষ্টগ্র্রাম) is (24&deg;16&rsquo;35.39&Prime;N, 91&deg; 7&rsquo;17.99&Prime;Ed)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Where to Stay</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>1. Hotel Tepantor Princess</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Jamirdia Master Bari, Bhaluka<br />\r\nMymenshingh, 2240 Purura, Bangladesh</p>\r\n\r\n<p>2. Hotel River View<br />\r\nStation Road, Kishoreganj</p>\r\n\r\n<p>3. Hotel shahina (Resident)<br />\r\nStation Road, Kishoreganj</p>\r\n\r\n<p>4. Bangladesh Guest House<br />\r\nStation Road, Kishoreganj</p>\r\n\r\n<p>5. Hotel Gangchil (Resident)<br />\r\nStation Road, Kishoreganj</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Things to do</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>The village is really wonderful for its scenic beauty. You can enjoy the gentle breeze that hits on the face after kissing the surface of the water. If you are a traveler, then you will always find out every bit of our traveling, interesting.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Eating Facilities</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>As well as you can find many more restaurant here for food.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Travel Tips</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Do not try to stay in the Haor at evening for it would be safe for you.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n', '[{\"image\":\"\\/uploads\\/images\\/1311264b129b263c67da529e0a17fe42.jpeg\"},{\"image\":\"\\/uploads\\/images\\/f45ac5e033bb25b444214be942536415.jpeg\"}]', '2023-11-05 19:36:10', '2023-11-11 19:07:36');
